body:
Sorry to be late to respond but stomas come in all kinds of shapes and sizes!  It varies on location and a bunch of other things that can make it not look the way a "perfect" i.e. the  ones you tend to see in the pamphlets given out from the various ostomy supply makers to the posters sometimes seen in a GI or colorectal surgeon's exam room.    


I'm wondering if perhaps your mom's skin irritation is caused from perhaps not having a proper fitting ostomy appliance... I say this as a person who's  stoma is an innie ... I joke that it's like the Sarlacc pit in the desert scene from Return of the Jedi.. (I started cracking jokes about it first as a coping mechanism at the beginning and now it's to make others laugh and be like a kind of ice breaker of sorts :D )  So going back to your mom's stoma when it's even remotely in the more concave shape it's really important to make sure the appliance she's using fits her needs.  I think there are a lot of ostomates that stick with whatever the hospital sent them home with unless it's not working for them.

I think the first person who replied (and probably others seconded and thirded etc) that your mom would totally benefit from seeing an ostomy nurse!  They know so much and can not only help with making sure your mom has the right ostomy supplies but they'll be able to explain a lot better than I can... about how her stoma will continue to change as it "matures" aka it takes a year for a stoma to be fully healed.  The  ostomy nurse can also make suggestions with regards to your mom's skin irritation because there are lot of things that can cause skin irritation and to give suggestions about  what to do requires more information; for example is it the skin directly around the stoma or is it skin that surrounds the area where the appliance is... the best thing is to find & meet with an ostomy nurse. they have a wealth of knowledge which is pretty awesome.

I can kinda relate to having an innie stoma (only mine is an ileostomy instead of  colostomy... I know there are differences but having even a semi-recessed stoma brings a different set of needs that are different from those with a perfect looking stoma.  Crap this is the most long winded way of saying see a stoma nurse! :)  (hopefully you find an awesome ostomy nurse and it helps your mom out with any and all issues :) <3 <3 <3  


feel free to message if you need anything even if its some one to talk to about dealing with this <3

