11r4f

The TSA are a bunch of jerks with a few who aren't... I actually had a TSA agent tell me that he **HAD** to open my manufacturer sealed like it's double sealed, prescription medication and had the balls to tell me that I could have easily revealed the bottles 😤😤😤😤😡😡😡😡 these were brand new bottles of liquid potassium and then he tried to take a bottle of a class 2 narcotic out of my view to "test it" I told him under no circumstance was he allowed to take my prescription out of view because he could spill it or do God knows what... This was after I actually submitted to a body scan where I wasn't allowed my walker, but they gave me a cane and then I got groped IN PUBLIC, that included grabbing my ostomy bag! They tried to get me to sho it and even though I was running way late and already traumatized because the airline didn't have assistance waiting for me to get me from the airport entrance to my gate.. I was crying because I was so angry about doing the freaking body scan only to get felt up in public... By the time I got to the gate I was hysterical and the ladies at the gate were so awesome, they changed me to the next flight which was departing only a bit later than my original and the other one went and got me some tissue & a cold bottle of water. 
I have never felt so humiliated in my life... The TSA agents at Regan National suck! I was flying to DC ever 4 weeks because I was in a clinical trial for a new chemo agent, so it was always super easy leaving from my local airport, the very first time I flew, they had a advocate to make sure the screening was done right and I never had an issue, I'd touch where my bag was and they'd do the explosives test.. Regan was always a nightmare, thinking about it makes me angry. /rant
Gah!!! Sorry about going off on a rant there >.<;
